      "actual_observations": [
        "Both disjoint selections were reviewed against their actual editorial song positions: raw[6,102) at83.083333\u201387.083333s, and raw[102,214) at254.625\u2013259.291667s. They are not loops or two generations.",
        "Hand/body mechanics and supported playing are source-passable in both portions: compact right-hand picking touches and connected left fretting/chord-position changes continue. The early portion is restrained finger/wrist activity, not broad energetic strumming or verified118BPM accuracy. The late portion gives gentler touches, controlled strokes, reduced shoulder effort and an absorbed head lift/listening quality; it does not become triumphant or an artificial still image.",
        "Both complete retained hand-contact sequences were inspected at native scale. Wider native windows cover the large late hand travel that partly left the original small inspection crops. Brief finger-line softness near raw98\u2013100 and169\u2013171 remains scoped motion texture, without an independent ghost hand, detached wrist or melted neck. Six-tuner headstock/paired pickups/strap/neutral pendant remain the same where visible.",
        "BLOCKING IMAGE FINDING: an invented round pale/dark glyph or ball appears in the otherwise unused lower-right background. Actual unscaled raw30,80 and125 corner extracts confirm it; it is absent by raw165. This is source content, not a Chromium control. Both requested source uses contain it, so neither is cleared unchanged.",
        "No full-length clean alternate can avoid that interval within this225-frame source. A tighter intentional portrait crop may exclude the empty-background corner, but a crop is not accepted here; its actual framing, action visibility, possible brief headstock-edge clipping and joins require new review. Native full raw178 shows the headstock/tuners reaching aboutx840."
      ],
